{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-luk-12-1","title":"Luke 12:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ preaches to his apostles to avoid hypocrisy, and fearfulness in publishing his doctrine; 13 warns the people to beware of covetousness, by the parable of the rich man who set up greater barns. 22 We must not be over careful of earthly things, 31 but seek the kingdom of God; 33 give alms; 35 be ready at a knock to open to our Lord whensoever he comes. 41 Christ's ministers are to see to their charges, 49 and look for persecution. 54 The people must take this time of grace; 57 because it is a fearful thing to die without reconciliation.</p>\n<p>an. 5:1,15; 6:17; Ac 21:20; *Gr: trode. 2Ki 7:17 first. 1Co 15:3; Jas 3:17 Beware. Mt 16:6-12; Mr 8:15-21; 1Co 5:7,8 which. 56; 11:44; Job 20:5; 27:8; 36:13; Isa 33:14; Jas 3:17; 1Pe 2:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-12-2","title":"Luke 12:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>8:17; Ec 12:14; Mt 10:26; Mr 4:22; Ro 2:16; 1Co 4:5; 2Co 5:10 Re 20:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-12-3","title":"Luke 12:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>whatsoever. Job 24:14,15; Ec 10:12,13,20; Mt 12:36; Jude 1:14,15 proclaimed.The houses in Judea being flat-roofed, with a balustrade round about, were used for the purpose of taking the air, sleeping, and prayer, and, it seems, for announcing things in the most public manner. So among the Turks, a crier announces the hours of public worship from the minaret or tower of the mosque.</p>\n<p>housetops. Mt 10:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-12-4","title":"Luke 12:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>my. So 5:1,16; Isa 41:8; Joh 15:14; Jas 2:23 Be. Isa 51:7-13; Jer 1:8,17; 26:14,15; Eze 2:6; Da 3:16,17; Mt 10:28 Ac 4:13; 20:24; Php 1:28; 1Pe 3:14; Re 2:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-12-5","title":"Luke 12:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>forewarn. Mr 13:23; 1Th 4:6 Fear. Pr 14:26; Jer 5:22; 10:7; Re 14:7; 15:4 power. Ps 9:17; Mt 10:28; 25:41,46; 2Pe 2:4; Re 20:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-12-6","title":"Luke 12:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>five. See Mt 10:29 and. 24,27; Ps 50:10,11; 113:5,6; 145:15,16; 147:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-12-7","title":"Luke 12:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>even. 21:18; 1Sa 14:45; 2Sa 14:11; Mt 10:30; Ac 27:34 ye are. Job 35:11; Ps 8:6; Isa 43:3,4; Mt 6:26; 10:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-12-8","title":"Luke 12:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Whosoever. 1Sa 2:30; Ps 119:46; Mt 10:32,33; Ro 10:9,10; 2Ti 2:12; 1Jo 2:23 Re 2:10,13; 3:4,5 confess. Mt 25:31-34; Jude 1:24,25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-12-9","title":"Luke 12:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>he. 9:26; Mt 10:33; Mr 8:38; Ac 3:13,14; 2Ti 2:12; Re 3:8 shall. 13:26,27; Mt 7:23; 25:12,31,41; 1Jo 2:23,28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-12-10","title":"Luke 12:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>23:34; Mt 12:31,32; Mr 3:28,29; 1Ti 1:13; Heb 6:4-8; 10:26-31 1Jo 5:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-12-11","title":"Luke 12:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":1